			//             at least half the handle width so the handle stays
			//             inside the bar at both ends.
			// `thumbW`  — handle width; the handle is centred on its position, so
			//             its transform offset is half this.
			// `fillCap` — how far the fill runs PAST the handle centre. The fill's
			//             end is a semicircle of radius (barHeight / 2); extending
			//             by exactly that radius puts the cap's centre on the
			//             handle's centre, so cap and handle are concentric and the
			//             fill visibly CONTAINS the handle at its right end. At
			//             MAX the fill then reaches the bar's right edge exactly.
			//             0 keeps the original shape, where the fill simply stops
			//             at the handle's centre line.
			rounded: { inset: 9, thumbW: 22, fillCap: 0 },
			// The capsule handle is a white circle sitting inside the fill's end cap,
			// leaving a ring of fill colour around it. These three numbers are tied to
			// the capsule bar height (28px, set on `.dms-sliderCapsule .dms-track`) and
			// to each other — retune them together:
			//   * fillCap = barHeight / 2 = 14, so at MAX the fill's end cap lands
			//     concentric with the handle AND the fill reaches the bar's right edge
			//     exactly (see fillWidthFor).
			//   * inset = 14 = fillCap, so the handle's travel ends where the cap
			//     centre sits; anything less would leave the fill short of the edge.
			//   * thumbW = 20 leaves a 4px ring ((28 - 20) / 2), the same ring the
