		// suppressed only while the rolling classes are on (see the
		// `text-overflow:clip` rule), and those come off after `DMS_ROLL_MS`. A
		// width transition as long as the roll would still be clipping the last
		// fraction of a pixel at that moment, so the incoming word would flash
		// "H..." one final time just as the roll ended — the exact defect the
		// suppression exists to remove, reappearing for a single frame. The 40ms
		// margin absorbs frame quantisation, and the difference between 220ms and
		// 260ms at a 3px change is not perceptible.
